{{- /* chezmoi:modify-template */ -}}

{{- /* https://paseo.sh/docs/configuration
       Paseo owns this file at runtime: `paseo daemon set-password` writes an
       auth hash, device pairing flips relay, and the Settings UI persists
       provider, profile, and feature choices. A modify-template so that state
       survives apply and only the choices this repo owns are pinned.

       daemon.mcp.injectIntoAgents is off upstream and is the reason to run
       Paseo here at all: agents it launches can then spawn and coordinate
       their own workers.

       relay stays off because reachability is Tailscale's job
       (.chezmoidata/tailscale.yaml), so the daemon never dials
       relay.paseo.sh. Paseo offers to enable it during device pairing;
       declining keeps this value, and a fresh home already writes false —
       pinned anyway because a config that omitted the field keeps the legacy
       relay-enabled behaviour.

       agents.skills.selection is an empty custom list, not `all`. The skills
       CLI owns ~/.agents/skills for every agent on this host and installs the
       paseo-* set from getpaseo/paseo
       (.chezmoidata/skills/providers-general.yaml). Paseo ships the same
       skills and re-converges them from its own bundle on startup, which
       would make two writers for one directory. An empty selection leaves its
       converger owning nothing; startup convergence never deletes, so the
       skills the CLI installed stay put.

       worktrees.root moves worktrees out of $PASEO_HOME, so .paseo/ is pure
       daemon state and tools.yaml can purge it wholesale. It points at the
       shared agent-worktree parent (path.data.worktree) rather than a
       Paseo-only directory, so every tool that can be pointed somewhere keeps
       its checkouts in one place. Paseo keeps its hashed per-project layout
       under this root and creates the directories on demand. Absolute so it
       never re-resolves against PASEO_HOME.

       Two tools stay out of that parent. Luvus derives worktree paths from
       LUVUS_HOME with no setting to override, and worktrunk deliberately puts
       worktrees beside their checkout for shell-driven work
       (dot_config/worktrunk/config.toml).

       Not pinned, deliberately:
       - daemon.listen, daemon.cors, app.baseUrl: Paseo writes its own values
         into a fresh home, and pinning them fights `paseo daemon start` flags.
       - daemon.mcp.enabled: already true by default.
       - daemon.enableTerminalAgentHooks: installing those hooks edits
         .claude/settings.json and .codex/hooks.json, which chezmoi manages.
         Off keeps one writer per path. */ -}}

{{- includeTemplate "config/merge" (dict
  "format" "json"
  "input" (dig "stdin" "" .chezmoi)
  "managed" (dict
    "$schema" "https://paseo.sh/schemas/paseo.config.v1.json"
    "version" 1
    "daemon" (dict
      "mcp" (dict
        "injectIntoAgents" true
      )
      "relay" (dict
        "enabled" false
      )
    )
    "worktrees" (dict
      "root" (joinPath .chezmoi.homeDir .path.data.worktree "paseo")
    )
    "agents" (dict
      "skills" (dict
        "selection" (dict
          "mode" "custom"
          "skills" (list)
        )
      )
    )
  )
) -}}
